    <li><strong>How products were checked:</strong> ClassTrack’s free limits were checked against the app’s code on {new Date(SITE.updated).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })}. Every other planner’s free plan comes from its official website, store listing or help pages, checked in October 2026 and linked in the sources.</li>
    <li><strong>How research was used:</strong> study advice is linked to peer-reviewed papers, listed below with DOIs. We report what each study measured and do not stretch it.</li>
    <li><strong>What we did not do:</strong> no paid placements, no made-up ratings or download counts, and no ranking a product higher because we make it without saying so.</li>
    <li><strong>Corrections:</strong> if a free plan has changed, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will update the page and its date. See the <a href="/about/#editorial">editorial policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="btn-row" style="margin:24px 0"><a class="btn" href={SITE.webUrl} rel="noopener">Try ClassTrack free on the web</a><a class="btn ghost" href={SITE.playUrl} rel="noopener">Get it on Google Play</a></div>
</Guide>
